          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮಜ್ಜಿಗೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಜ್ಜಿಗೆ — majjige — \"buttermilk\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಜ್ಜಿಗೆ (majjige) is shared with Tamil maccikai and Telugu majjiga, \"buttermilk\" (DEDR 4630). DEDR 4630 suggests, with a query, that it may be a loan from Indo-Aryan, comparing Prakrit majjiā, a curd dish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
